exec bin/codex-review 'Review branch codex/kernel-probes (worktree /home/ubuntu/work/gemma-wt/codex-kernel-probes), diff codex/kernel-setup-fix5...codex/kernel-probes (one commit 63127c8), plus the bundle bundles/31b/v001 vs bundles/31b/v000. Spec: eval/plans/006.md "Addendum" + ops/decisions/034-009-scorer-setup-path.md item 2. Changes: eval/kaggle/agent_timing.py adds P1 stock_setup_probe (per task, BEFORE the emulated run and outside its times/Phase-1 clock; mirrors eval/tools/stock_subprocess_setup_timing.py; must call the STOCK install_test_dependencies via _timing_original even though patch_subprocess_deps rebinds it), P2 platform_probe (once, header; docker which/sock, DNS in a thread with 10 s join, ONE TCP connect to pypi.org:443 timeout 10 s, NO payload; internet is OFF on the kernel), P3 llm_calls (per usage-bearing trace entry). eval/kaggle/timing_summary.py adds gate_mode minus-image: (b) max(phase1_wall_seconds - image_emulation_seconds) <= cap*60+37, (c) not gated, plus a probes block and decision_note. New tests eval/tests/test_kernel_probes.py (117 pass with test_agent_timing + test_setup_check). Check: (1) P1 cannot change the measured task (shared state, ContextVar, sys.modules rebinding, page cache, leftover venvs/disk, exceptions) and can never abort the run; worst-case P1 duration (SubprocessManager timeout 120 s per exec) vs KERNEL_BUDGET_SECONDS 6000 and should_stop; (2) P2 sends nothing and cannot hang beyond ~20 s; any compliance concern with a DNS lookup/TCP SYN from a Kaggle kernel with internet off; (3) P3 row semantics (does ADK attach usage once per model event? see adk_eval_core/tracing/trace.py consume_usage) and no task text/patch content in rows; (4) gate arithmetic and failure on missing measurements; default gate mode unchanged; (5) 31b-v001: only max_time_minutes 5 -> 4.0 (+ comment arithmetic: (240+7+221.6)/60*125+30 = 1006 > 660 under H3; (240+7+30)/60*125+30 = 607) and max_output_tokens 16384 -> 8192 at both occurrences; dist